# The runtime/mission-route test harness is bash + python. On Windows checkouts,
# core.autocrlf rewrites these to CRLF, which makes WSL bash fail with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name" (a trailing \r on `set -euo pipefail`)
# and breaks python route/script parsing — so the mission harness cannot run.
# The blobs are already LF; these rules stop autocrlf from mangling them on
# checkout, making the harness runnable in a Windows + WSL checkout.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.script   text eol=lf
*.env      text eol=lf
*.gdb      text eol=lf
